          "severity": "medium",
          "category": "maintainability",
          "confidence": 0.88,
          "description": "The `committed traces` describe block calls `readdirSync` at module evaluation time (outside any `beforeEach`/`it`). If the `traces/` directory is missing (e.g., a fresh checkout before any trace has been committed, or a different working directory), the test file throws at import time, crashing the entire test suite with a cryptic Node error rather than a clear test failure. The test immediately below guards `traceFiles.length > 0`, but it never runs if the directory doesn't exist.",
          "suggestedFix": "Wrap the `readdirSync` in a try/catch or use `existsSync` first, returning an empty array when the directory is absent, so the `'finds at least one committed trace'` test fails with a clear message instead of the whole suite crashing."
        }
      ],
      "validationResult": "ok",
      "endedAt": "2026-07-17T10:31:16.215Z"
